"Pharvaris N.V., a late-stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the development and commercialization of therapies for rare diseases with unmet needs covering angioedema and other bradykinin-mediated diseases. The company develops deucrictibant, a small molecule bradykinin B2-receptor antagonist to treat attacks due to bradykinin-mediated angioedema, including hereditary angioedema (HAE) and acquired angioedema due to C1-inhibitor deficiency (AAE-C1INH), which is in phase 3, as well as in phase 3 trials for treatment and prophylaxis of HAE attacks; and extended-release tablet and immediate-release capsule formulation of deucrictibant. Pharvaris N.V. was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in Zug, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Berndt Axel Edvard Modig CPA, M.B.A. | Co-Founder, CEO & Executive Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 148 people.","financial_summary":["Pharvaris N.V. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.4B market cap.","The company is burning through $151M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -4697.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $18.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA o